ST Internal Reference: 202753

[ASEHSTM - 2025-03-03T10:17:44Z]
Hello @carlo-dev-git,

After further analysis, we confirmed that the use of the operator = is unnecessary for all HAL CAN processes. The requirement for this operator is limited to the interrupt process, where the fix has been successfully implemented. Below is the macro that addresses the race condition issue:


#define __HAL_CAN_CLEAR_FLAG(__HANDLE__, __FLAG__) \
  ((((__FLAG__) >> 8U) == 5U) ? (((__HANDLE__)->Instance->TSR) = (1U << ((__FLAG__) & CAN_FLAG_MASK))) : \
   (((__FLAG__) >> 8U) == 2U) ? (((__HANDLE__)->Instance->RF0R) = (1U << ((__FLAG__) & CAN_FLAG_MASK))) : \
   (((__FLAG__) >> 8U) == 4U) ? (((__HANDLE__)->Instance->RF1R) = (1U << ((__FLAG__) & CAN_FLAG_MASK))) : \
   (((__FLAG__) >> 8U) == 1U) ? (((__HANDLE__)->Instance->MSR) = (1U << ((__FLAG__) & CAN_FLAG_MASK))) : 0U)


Thank you,
With Regards,

